---
# Managed by c-coding-standards skill (resources/lint/clang-tidy/.clang-tidy)
# clang-tidy config is YAML and is auto-discovered up the directory tree. [3](https://lindevs.com/generate-json-compilation-database-using-cmake)[4](https://developers.redhat.com/blog/2020/03/26/static-analysis-in-gcc-10)

Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  misc-definitions-in-headers,
  misc-unused-parameters

# Fail CI on any enabled diagnostic.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'

# Only report diagnostics in your project headers (adjust to your tree).
# clang-tidy supports header filtering via HeaderFilterRegex. [3](https://lindevs.com/generate-json-compilation-database-using-cmake)
HeaderFilterRegex: '^(src|include|drivers)/'

# Keep formatting out of clang-tidy (style is handled by other tooling).
FormatStyle: none

CheckOptions:
  # BARR-C "always braces" support: require braces even for short statements.
  - key: readability-braces-around-statements.ShortStatementLines
    value: '0'

  # If any checks refer to NULL as a macro (helps tool understand NULL usage).
  - key: modernize-use-nullptr.NullMacros
    value: 'NULL'
...
